// Materials (D101, docs/design/ship-model.md §3.1; read by sim::materials).
//
// Units: density kg/m³, modulus and strength Pa, conductivity W/(m·K),
// specific heat J/(kg·K), temperatures K, cost USD/kg of mill product,
// era = year of first flight use. Strength is a table against temperature
// (yield and ultimate; a brittle material's yield equals its ultimate),
// interpolated linearly and held at its ends; nothing is carried at or above
// destruction_k. Emissivity and absorptivity are the bare surface's (a
// finish below overrides them). fatigue_exponent is the S–N curve's m
// (cycles ∝ S^-m).
//
// Provenance: CORE wrote this first set from well-known handbook values
// (2026-10-26) and named each material's sources; `verify` lists the fields
// given from memory and still to be checked against those sources. The data
// workstream (DATA) edits values and empties `verify` as it checks them.
